concept:crimes-internationally-protected-persons-act-1976-article-10 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10 1. States Parties shall afford one another the greatest measure of assistance"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:article-10 ;
    values:originalText "in connexion with criminal proceedings brought in respect of the crimes set forth in article 2, including the supply of all evidence at their disposal necessary for the proceedings. 2. The provisions of paragraph 1 of this article shall not affect obligations concerning mutual judicial assistance embodied in any other treaty.  Schedule  Convention on the prevention and punishment of crimes against internationally protected persons, including diplomatic agents  Crimes (Internationally Protected Persons) Act 1976  Compilation date: 10/3/16 Registered: 26/5/16" ;
    skos:definition "in connexion with criminal proceedings brought in respect of the crimes set forth in article 2, including the supply of all evidence at their disposal necessary for the proceedings. 2. The provisions of paragraph 1 of this article shall not affect obligations concerning mutual judicial assistance embodied in any other treaty.  Schedule  Convention on the prevention and punishment of crimes against internationally protected persons, including diplomatic agents  Crimes (Internationally Protected Persons) Act 1976  Compilation date: 10/3/16 Registered: 26/5/16"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "56eb5466b90a05086d093fe221f93882f7712f59cd22bacf5efd29c0ce7353d8" ;
